sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS 4 + R1-R4 (process.stop shape: 209, @swamp/ssh, full intent as inputs). Update shares operation-process-create.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 1-22 (cfgmgmt file/systemd/docker_*, no shipped scripts, no report step).
  %% Decided: Nick 2026-11-02, a Docker Process runs as one plain docker run through @swamp/ssh exec; pull with cfgmgmt docker_image, check with the docker_container check.
  %% Rule 23: 2026-11-03 required-only main path.
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: process:update
  %% kind: process.update
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  alt Project definition update
    CLI->>GW: Update definition<br/>only supplied fields
    Note over GW: Merge and validate<br/>preserve omitted values
    %%> Changing runtime replaces the runtime specification; it requires the new runtime's command and fields.
    %%> Empty maps and lists clear the supplied field. Preset command and metadata remain canonical.
    GW-->>CLI: Updated or refused<br/>validation result
    %%> A later default development container deploy applies the definition to its linked Processes; new clones inherit it.
  else Installed Process update
  CLI->>GW: process:update 418
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit process:update 418`
  %%> - syntax: `process:update <process> [--runtime=systemd|docker] [--command=ARG ...] [--image=IMAGE] [options]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the numeric Process ID; without options it re-applies the recorded definition
  %%> Optional:
  %%> - `--runtime`, `--command`, `--image`, `--working-directory`, `--environment`, `--port`, `--volume`, `--restart`, `--keep-alive`, `--no-restart-on-deploy`, `--user` change only the fields they name; omitted fields keep their recorded value
  %%> - these flags change the rendered definition, not the steps; the branches below follow recorded state, such as a retired runtime after `--runtime`
  %%> - `--idempotency-key` reuses a task start; `--json` returns JSON
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>keep old spec · #5130
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Process's Node
  %%> - a Valkey Database server follows the [image-update rule and validation order](/reference/database-servers#update-a-valkey-servers-image)
  %%> - a Route that points to this Process keeps the same listener, else `process.route_upstream_changed`
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the new unit or container rendered; secret environment values pushed to the vault key `process-update-operation-5130`
  %%> - the stored definition keeps the old spec until the run succeeds
  %%> - development container definitions store supported command names and resolve them when rendering; capture adopts only a compatible unlinked same-name Process, keeping its id and desired state
  %%> - task #5130 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-process-create
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); every step runs there
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `kind`: process.update
  %%> - the rendered unit, or the container definition without its environment values
  %%> - the desired state, required mounts, and a retired name when the runtime or name changed, all from recorded state
  %%> - vault key names for the environment, never the values
  %%> - the Node's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> Checked by the input schema:
  %%> - no step reads or re-checks the intent
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5130
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  opt certificate account home is not recorded
    SW->>N: Check the account<br/>ssh exec · getent
  end
  Note over SW: Prepare the definition<br/>public rendering only
  %%> Resolves the observed home in certificate paths and shapes Docker argv; no Node effects.
  opt required mounts set and running
    SW->>N: Check required mounts<br/>ssh exec · stat
  end
  opt runtime or name changed
    SW->>N: Remove the retired unit<br/>native destroy workflow
  end
  opt environment values set
    SW->>N: Write the environment<br/>cfgmgmt/file · 0600
    %%> vault.get content, root owner; no secret in public run data.
  end
  opt Vite dev Process
    SW->>N: Publish the dev route<br/>native Vite workflow
    %%> Publishes the Vite environment before its unit starts.
  end
  alt systemd
    SW->>N: Apply the unit<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd.apply
    %%> Publishes unitFile, reloads on content change, and applies the admitted boot and active state.
    opt previous activation is pending
      SW->>N: Reload systemd<br/>ssh exec · daemon-reload
      %%> Covers a prior publish that failed before daemon-reload.
    end
    opt desired state is stopped
      SW->>N: Stop the unit<br/>ssh exec · stop
      %%> Cancels activating units too; pinned apply stops only active units.
    end
    opt changed unit is already running
      SW->>N: Restart if changed<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd.restart
      %%> Pinned apply leaves an already active process running after unitFile changes.
    end
    SW->>N: Check the unit<br/>cfgmgmt/systemd.check
  else Docker
    SW->>N: Pull the image<br/>cfgmgmt/docker_image
    SW->>N: Remove the old container<br/>ssh exec · docker rm -f
    SW->>N: Replace the container<br/>ssh exec · docker run -d
    %%> One argv command, env-file, workdir, image and exact command arguments.
    opt desired state is stopped
      SW->>N: Stop the container<br/>ssh exec · docker stop
      %%> The detached run starts it; this step converges a stopped creation or update.
    end
    SW->>N: Check the container<br/>cfgmgmt/docker_container
  end
  opt Vite dev Process, running
    SW->>N: Check the listener<br/>ssh exec · ss
    SW->>N: Mark it awake<br/>cfgmgmt/file
  end
  SW->>N: Verify it runs<br/>native assert
  %%> Requires the admitted active/stopped state and boot policy, and any Vite listener.
  alt Process running
    N-->>SW: active (running)
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the Process has its desired state
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the end check's output; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Store the new spec<br/>Process 418: active
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the stored definition becomes the new spec
    %%> - task #5130 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - SSH fails, a required mount is missing, or the state does not match
    %%> How:
    %%> - the failing step ends the run with its own exit code; there is no report step
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its exit code, mapped to `error_code`
    Note over GW: Keep the old spec<br/>task failed · rerun converges
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 418 keeps its old definition and is marked failed
    %%> - work done on the Node stays; nothing was copied, so nothing needs cleanup
    %%> - run the update again to converge: each behavior skips state that is already right
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5130
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
  end
